      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I’m really glad you said that out loud—that takes a lot of courage. You’re not a shell; you’re someone in the middle of a brutal transition, and grief can make us feel invisible. The fact that you can name this emptiness means the person is still in there, just buried under the weight of loss. If you can, try to do one small thing today that connects you to who you were—even just a memory, a song, or a photo. You don’t have to fix it all at once, but you don’t have to face it alone either.",
